qcommon: pass vmMain arguments as an array on all but 32-bit x86

VM_Call() hands the interpreter and the compiled VM a pointer to callnum,
(int *)&callnum, on id386 and idsparc, assuming that the variadic int
arguments follow callnum in memory as 32-bit slots. On 32-bit SPARC gcc
spills the register arguments of a variadic function to consecutive
words, so this happened to work. On 64-bit SPARC (sparcv9, idsparc as
well) arguments occupy 8-byte slots, and the QVM receives garbage:
"UI_SetActiveMenu: bad enum" in the UI, with the interpreter (vm_ui 1)
and the sparc compiler (vm_ui 2) alike.

Copy the arguments into the int array as on every other platform; keep
the shortcut for 32-bit x86 only, where the cdecl stack layout guarantees
it. The array path already serves PPC, x86_64 and the rest.

Same fix as ioquake3 (ioq3 has the same code); for SP and MP.
vm_* 1 and 2; x86_64 builds take the same path as before.

Upstream: not submitted yet (patch prepared for github.com/ioquake/ioq3).

--- iortcw-438e7d413b5f7277187c35b032eb0ef9093ae778/SP/code/qcommon/vm.c.orig
+++ iortcw-438e7d413b5f7277187c35b032eb0ef9093ae778/SP/code/qcommon/vm.c
@@ -852,7 +852,7 @@
                             args[4],  args[5],  args[6], args[7],
                             args[8],  args[9], args[10], args[11]);
 	} else {
-#if ( id386 || idsparc ) && !defined __clang__ // calling convention doesn't need conversion in some cases
+#if id386 && !defined __clang__ // calling convention doesn't need conversion in some cases
 #ifndef NO_VM_COMPILED
 		if ( vm->compiled )
 			r = VM_CallCompiled( vm, (int*)&callnum );
